WEBVTT

00:02.970 --> 00:05.280
I'm the same as usual!

00:05.280 --> 00:08.380
You're the one who needs to calm down!

00:08.940 --> 00:11.830
We're getting the gold at the Nationals.

02:01.640 --> 02:05.210
Did you get the order form for
the SunFes outfits from Taki-sensei?

02:05.210 --> 02:06.130
Yeah.

02:06.130 --> 02:09.180
We're reusing last year's data.

02:09.180 --> 02:11.100
Pardon us.

02:11.750 --> 02:14.230
What about you, though, Kumiko?

02:14.230 --> 02:15.230
<b>Music Room</b>

02:14.230 --> 02:15.240
What about me?

02:15.240 --> 02:16.390
Your career path.

02:17.830 --> 02:19.160
Dunno.

02:19.520 --> 02:22.340
I don't have time to think about it.

02:22.340 --> 02:23.810
Why not music school?

02:23.810 --> 02:25.520
Like Yoroizuka-senpai.

02:25.520 --> 02:28.330
It's not such an easy decision.

02:28.330 --> 02:29.850
There's so much to prepare.

02:30.480 --> 02:34.750
I'd like it if you continued music.

02:36.280 --> 02:37.920
What was that?

02:37.920 --> 02:39.290
That was a rare moment.

02:40.340 --> 02:41.670
President!

02:41.670 --> 02:43.160
Good morning!

02:42.410 --> 02:43.850
Good morning.

02:43.850 --> 02:44.670
Morning.

02:44.670 --> 02:46.190
You're up early again.

02:46.190 --> 02:46.890
Yup.

02:46.890 --> 02:49.720
Sally says she wants to work 
on the competition pieces.

02:49.720 --> 02:50.450
Yeah?

02:50.450 --> 02:53.750
She's such a tryhard. Sheesh.

02:53.750 --> 02:55.420
Of course I am.

02:55.420 --> 02:57.500
We're all going for the 
gold at the Nationals.

02:57.500 --> 02:59.060
That's my Sally!

02:59.060 --> 03:01.340
Always such an ambitious Annie.

03:01.340 --> 03:03.080
You're not getting a reaction 
out of me for that anymore.

03:03.080 --> 03:04.920
You're the leader of the 
first-years, after all.

03:04.920 --> 03:06.810
Maybe you'll be the president 
in a couple years.

03:06.810 --> 03:07.550
Right, President?

03:07.550 --> 03:10.160
That's still way in the future.

03:10.160 --> 03:13.270
You don't want to be thinking 
about that yet either, do you?

03:13.270 --> 03:14.510
I don't.

03:14.510 --> 03:17.530
Well, yeah, but...

03:18.700 --> 03:22.450
You can't help but have high 
hopes for your dear child.

03:22.450 --> 03:24.110
Who are you calling your child?

03:23.430 --> 03:24.930
<b>10 days 
until SunFes!</b>

03:26.010 --> 03:29.930
<b>Episode 3</b>

03:26.010 --> 03:29.930
<b>Blue Prelude</b>

03:30.510 --> 03:34.060
Trombones! Yoshizawa-san! 
Your arms are drooping!

03:34.060 --> 03:36.430
Keep them parallel to the ground!

03:36.430 --> 03:37.220
Okay!

03:37.580 --> 03:40.890
Saxophones! Koumoto-san! 
Raise your feet more!

03:40.890 --> 03:41.700
Yes!

03:43.070 --> 03:44.820
The selection piece this year is pretty challenging.
 I don't think we'll have time to take care of the 
kids who can't keep up at practice.

03:43.700 --> 03:46.560
<i>The selection piece this 
year is pretty challenging.</i>

03:46.560 --> 03:50.730
<i>I don't think we'll have time to take care 
of the kids who can't keep up at practice.</i>

03:51.330 --> 03:54.130
<i>I don't want anyone to drop out, though.</i>

03:51.330 --> 03:56.590
I don't want anyone to drop out, though. 
We aren't Kitauji unless we're all there.

03:54.130 --> 03:56.600
<i>We aren't Kitauji unless we're all there.</i>

03:57.000 --> 03:58.060
You're off.

03:58.060 --> 03:58.700
Yes.

03:58.700 --> 04:01.950
<i>That's a platitude, though.</i>

03:59.590 --> 04:01.880
That's a platitude, though.

04:01.950 --> 04:04.320
<i>If someone says they want 
to quit, I can't stop them.</i>

04:01.950 --> 04:04.320
If someone says they want 
to quit, I can't stop them.

04:04.320 --> 04:07.330
<i>Do you think you're being kind?</i>

04:04.320 --> 04:07.330
Do you think you're being kind?

04:07.330 --> 04:08.610
Stop!

04:10.270 --> 04:12.220
Takekawa-san of the horns.

04:12.540 --> 04:14.190
Your steps are off again.

04:14.190 --> 04:15.090
R-Right.

04:15.090 --> 04:17.220
You put the person behind you in 
danger when you aren't together.

04:17.220 --> 04:18.890
I told you before.

04:18.890 --> 04:19.830
Right.

04:20.350 --> 04:21.610
I'm sorry.

04:26.740 --> 04:28.530
Step out of the line, please.

04:29.240 --> 04:30.900
I'm sorry.

04:32.360 --> 04:35.980
Also, Hariya-san, euphonium, 
your movement is clumsy.

04:35.980 --> 04:37.470
And your strides are too small.

04:37.470 --> 04:38.080
Okay.

04:38.080 --> 04:39.700
Focus, please.

04:42.140 --> 04:44.970
All right, let's run it again.

04:45.710 --> 04:46.630
Yes.

04:50.430 --> 04:51.930
<b>Trying
 on
 clothes. 
Keep
 out.</b>

04:50.430 --> 04:51.930
<b>Concert 
Band</b>

04:55.750 --> 04:58.550
You look good in anything, Reina.

04:58.550 --> 05:00.520
You look good, too.

05:00.520 --> 05:03.070
I mean, well...

05:03.520 --> 05:04.770
Thanks.

05:04.770 --> 05:06.480
You have nothing to worry about.

05:06.480 --> 05:09.460
You're plenty cute, Kumiko-senpai.

05:10.260 --> 05:11.770
You, too, Kanade-chan.

05:11.770 --> 05:13.570
I know.

05:14.840 --> 05:16.290
Kumiko-chan...

05:16.290 --> 05:19.740
My shirt is a bit too small.

05:27.680 --> 05:28.870
Kumiko-chan?

05:29.960 --> 05:32.680
Ask the person in charge of uniforms. 
They can change it for you.

05:32.680 --> 05:34.580
Ah, okay.

05:34.580 --> 05:35.580
I'll do that.

05:35.580 --> 05:36.130
Okay.

05:36.130 --> 05:40.040
Kuroe-senpai seems like the type 
who would be popular with men.

05:40.040 --> 05:42.280
I'm sure she's popular.

05:42.280 --> 05:43.410
She's cute, too.

05:43.410 --> 05:44.770
Cuter than me?

05:45.730 --> 05:47.690
In a different way.

05:47.690 --> 05:49.360
I get it.

05:49.360 --> 05:51.380
Kanade-chan's more of a cat.

05:51.650 --> 05:52.280
Meow.

05:52.280 --> 05:54.410
Ooh, the animal series.

05:54.410 --> 05:55.660
What's that?

05:55.660 --> 05:58.380
Midori-chan's likes comparing us to animals.

05:58.380 --> 05:59.310
Huh.

05:59.310 --> 06:00.640
What about Kousaka-senpai, then?

06:00.640 --> 06:02.560
Reina-chan's...

06:02.560 --> 06:03.590
A white snake, maybe.

06:03.590 --> 06:04.610
Snake?

06:04.610 --> 06:06.690
Cute, but sometimes a bit scary.

06:06.690 --> 06:13.030
Kaho-chan's an alpaca, Yayoi-chan's a 
penguin, and Suzume-chan's a panda.

06:13.030 --> 06:14.390
I see.

06:14.390 --> 06:15.720
What about Mama-chan, then?

06:17.250 --> 06:19.630
I think Mayu-chan's a jellyfish.

06:19.630 --> 06:22.540
She looks pretty and like she's 
just drifting through the water,

06:22.540 --> 06:24.450
but if she stings, it hurts.

06:24.450 --> 06:27.450
Be careful not to get stung.

06:30.170 --> 06:33.690
President, may we have a word?

06:34.600 --> 06:38.070
How does it make sense that you 
go home first if you're bad?

06:38.070 --> 06:40.840
Sally stays back to practice every day!

06:40.840 --> 06:45.230
It's not like they're slacking 
during practice, though, are they?

06:45.230 --> 06:47.310
Well, yeah, but...

06:47.310 --> 06:50.750
Wouldn't you practice on your 
own if you need to catch up?

06:50.750 --> 06:55.920
I get where you're coming from, but 
individual practice is individual practice.

06:56.210 --> 06:58.110
I'll go talk to them.

06:58.110 --> 07:01.130
Thanks for putting so 
much thought into this.

07:05.830 --> 07:07.940
Huh? Sally...

07:07.940 --> 07:10.560
She usually stays behind.

07:16.300 --> 07:18.200
Good morning.

07:18.590 --> 07:20.450
You're the first to arrive again.

07:20.760 --> 07:22.400
Thank you.

07:22.400 --> 07:24.900
You're here early, too, Sensei.

07:24.900 --> 07:25.830
Yes.

07:25.830 --> 07:28.400
I have lots to do.

07:30.830 --> 07:33.770
Growing up seems hard.

07:33.770 --> 07:37.500
Do you not look forward to 
becoming an adult, Oumae-san?

07:37.500 --> 07:42.900
Well, more like... I can't 
imagine what it's like.

07:43.530 --> 07:45.530
What about you?

07:46.230 --> 07:49.880
I was more looking forward to it than not.

07:50.400 --> 07:52.740
I told myself that, as an adult,

07:52.740 --> 07:56.910
I could work and become someone 
that others look up to.

07:58.100 --> 08:04.300
But I tend to think I'm still 
more of an overgrown child.

08:05.340 --> 08:07.130
<i>You</i> think that?

08:07.610 --> 08:08.530
Yes.

08:09.440 --> 08:11.920
Now that I've gotten older,

08:12.300 --> 08:17.870
I find that whether you're an adult or a 
child depends on the environment you're in.

08:19.060 --> 08:21.060
<b>Milk Coffee</b>

08:23.880 --> 08:27.130
We shouldn't be wasting Taki-sensei's time.

08:27.130 --> 08:29.810
Even I don't get to talk to him much.

08:30.210 --> 08:31.850
Good morning.

08:33.220 --> 08:33.860
Morning.

08:34.220 --> 08:36.250
Is Kousaka-senpai here, too?

08:36.740 --> 08:38.680
Good morning!

08:38.680 --> 08:39.570
Morning.

08:40.320 --> 08:41.920
Oumae-senpai...

08:48.260 --> 08:54.920
Do you enjoy the club?

08:59.430 --> 09:02.310
I'm sorry, never mind.

09:02.870 --> 09:03.790
Um...

09:03.790 --> 09:07.940
Senpai, could I discuss something with you?

09:07.940 --> 09:09.120
Sure.

09:09.560 --> 09:12.710
Sorry, I'll see you at practice.

09:13.040 --> 09:16.970
You're asking me to be alone 
with Kousaka-senpai?!

09:20.110 --> 09:22.560
Sally-chan...

09:22.560 --> 09:24.150
Sorry, I...

09:24.720 --> 09:26.360
I'll be practicing.

09:31.790 --> 09:33.050
So...

09:33.450 --> 09:36.570
There's something I wanted to ask you.

09:36.570 --> 09:37.500
What's that?

09:37.930 --> 09:41.590
Are you and the vice president 
in a relationship?!

09:42.670 --> 09:43.350
Wha?

09:43.350 --> 09:46.060
Well, it's a big deal among the first-years.

09:46.060 --> 09:47.930
We're sure you're dating!

09:47.930 --> 09:49.190
<i>That's</i> what you want to discuss?

09:49.190 --> 09:52.640
Y'know, you were so lovey-dovey 
walking together the other day!

09:52.950 --> 09:54.810
You live in the same condo.

09:54.810 --> 09:56.020
You're basically married!

09:56.020 --> 09:58.150
Hang on! You're jumping to conclusions!

09:58.150 --> 09:59.980
You aren't dating?

09:59.980 --> 10:00.480
We aren't.

10:00.480 --> 10:01.690
Really?

10:01.690 --> 10:03.610
Really really.

10:03.610 --> 10:04.830
Oh...

10:05.310 --> 10:08.990
I was so hoping things 
would get interesting.

10:08.990 --> 10:09.790
Wait!

10:09.790 --> 10:10.820
Jeez.

10:10.820 --> 10:13.290
And here I was, wondering what 
you wanted to talk about.

10:13.290 --> 10:14.890
Oh, no.

10:14.890 --> 10:17.500
That's just some random gossip.

10:17.500 --> 10:19.650
I still have something 
else I want to discuss.

10:19.650 --> 10:20.930
I see.

10:20.930 --> 10:21.870
Yes.

10:22.210 --> 10:26.510
Senpai, you might have noticed...

10:27.780 --> 10:33.270
At this rate, the first-years 
are going to boycott the club.

10:39.940 --> 10:44.040
It might be more accurate to 
call it a mass resignation.

10:44.040 --> 10:49.030
You know how Kousaka-senpai's as strict 
with beginners as everyone else.

10:49.040 --> 10:51.290
Thoughts about the future

10:51.290 --> 10:54.960
So the first-years are afraid of Reina?

10:54.960 --> 10:55.880
No.

10:55.880 --> 10:59.600
In fact, the experienced members like her.

10:59.600 --> 11:01.410
Like, they admire her.

11:01.820 --> 11:05.720
So the first-years have mixed opinions.

11:10.370 --> 11:13.090
<i>Mass resignation...</i>

11:18.900 --> 11:19.400
<b>Resignation</b>

11:33.650 --> 11:38.690
And Reina's trying her best 
to make us better, too.

11:44.150 --> 11:46.560
Everyone wants to get good.

11:52.190 --> 11:54.190
We aren't Kitauji unless we're all there.

11:56.700 --> 12:00.030
"We aren't Kitauji unless 
we're all there," huh?

12:01.490 --> 12:07.310
<i>But what happened then happened 
before we could even react.</i>

12:04.950 --> 12:07.950
<b>SunFes in 
7 days</b>

12:13.200 --> 12:16.540
Something happened! 
Something definitely happened!

12:16.540 --> 12:18.130
Something?

12:18.130 --> 12:22.600
Suzume-chan and Kaho-chan and Yayoi-chan 
are all away on the same day.

12:23.170 --> 12:25.320
They've been contacting you, though, right?

12:25.320 --> 12:26.750
Hazuki-senpai.

12:26.750 --> 12:27.840
Riririn!

12:27.840 --> 12:28.910
What's wrong?

12:28.910 --> 12:32.530
Sally-chan's apparently away today.

12:32.530 --> 12:35.190
So all four of them, then?

12:35.450 --> 12:39.740
One of the clarinets told me they're sick.

12:39.740 --> 12:42.860
But that they might go ahead and quit...

12:42.860 --> 12:44.700
Oh, no way.

12:44.700 --> 12:45.650
Why?

12:45.650 --> 12:49.940
They said it just kinda 
seemed like they would.

12:54.100 --> 12:56.850
I asked for their addresses,

12:56.850 --> 13:00.300
but I think you might want to talk to them, 
since you're in charge of the first-years.

13:01.520 --> 13:02.610
All right.

13:02.610 --> 13:03.800
I'll go, too.

13:04.300 --> 13:05.510
You, too?

13:05.510 --> 13:07.590
Just in case, you know.

13:07.910 --> 13:09.370
Sorry, Kanade-chan.

13:09.370 --> 13:10.730
Could you take care of it here?

13:10.730 --> 13:12.370
Of course.

13:12.370 --> 13:13.360
Umm...

13:13.360 --> 13:15.940
Is it worth making such a big deal about?

13:16.520 --> 13:19.690
People quit clubs all the time.

13:19.690 --> 13:21.710
You don't need to go after them.

13:21.710 --> 13:23.810
They're one of us, though.

13:23.810 --> 13:27.580
People who want to quit get 
to be free from the club.

13:27.580 --> 13:32.080
Everyone staying behind gets to focus 
on performances without worry.

13:32.370 --> 13:34.400
I think it's a good thing.

13:35.270 --> 13:37.170
It's just a club, after all.

13:37.930 --> 13:40.720
I don't think you need to cling to it.

13:41.740 --> 13:44.100
Huh, should I not have said that?

13:44.370 --> 13:48.710
Nah, I was just thinking you 
rarely say anything so extreme.

13:48.710 --> 13:50.470
I'm sorry.

13:50.470 --> 13:52.300
That was a bit much.

13:52.300 --> 13:55.220
I can be like this sometimes.

13:55.220 --> 13:56.360
Don't mind me.

13:59.520 --> 14:02.620
I never would have thought 
she lives in a temple.

14:02.620 --> 14:05.610
It's a washnut tree.

14:05.610 --> 14:08.100
You know a lot.

14:08.100 --> 14:11.320
Nah, my grandma just had the 
same tree at her place.

14:11.320 --> 14:13.120
Oh yeah?

14:15.130 --> 14:16.420
P-President!

14:16.420 --> 14:17.260
Huh?

14:17.260 --> 14:19.990
I thought this was Sally-chan's place.

14:19.990 --> 14:21.010
No, it is.

14:21.010 --> 14:26.960
W-We've been helping out 
here every now and then.

14:26.960 --> 14:28.040
Huh.

14:28.040 --> 14:29.190
Also, shrine maiden uniforms!

14:29.190 --> 14:30.510
So cute.

14:30.510 --> 14:33.680
Wait, so that means Sally-chan's here, too?

14:33.680 --> 14:34.260
Yes.

14:34.260 --> 14:35.600
She's resting inside.

14:36.170 --> 14:38.320
Is she <i>that</i> sick?!

14:38.320 --> 14:39.360
S-Sorry.

14:39.360 --> 14:40.730
Kumiko.

14:40.730 --> 14:44.370
No, I didn't mean to do that, but...

14:50.680 --> 14:51.760
I'm sorry.

14:51.760 --> 14:52.970
No, it's fine.

14:52.970 --> 14:54.280
The thing is...

14:56.770 --> 14:58.830
Thanks for having us.

14:59.750 --> 15:01.580
Just give me a moment.

15:01.580 --> 15:02.250
Okay.

15:02.990 --> 15:04.530
Sure, okay.

15:05.480 --> 15:07.120
Senpai, come in.

15:08.640 --> 15:10.090
Thanks.

15:10.090 --> 15:11.670
Piano?

15:12.250 --> 15:13.440
Sally-chan.

15:15.670 --> 15:17.520
Sorry for barging in.

15:17.520 --> 15:18.430
A piano?!

15:18.430 --> 15:19.760
It's so cute.

15:20.020 --> 15:23.530
No, I'm sorry I worried you.

15:23.530 --> 15:26.910
Oh, so you really were sick.

15:26.910 --> 15:28.270
Are you all right?

15:30.070 --> 15:33.270
I said I'm fine, but...

15:33.270 --> 15:36.650
Suzume said we should all go home together.

15:37.420 --> 15:38.810
I see.

15:39.390 --> 15:40.520
Are you well?

15:41.460 --> 15:42.230
Yes.

15:42.230 --> 15:44.200
My fever's gone now, too.

15:44.200 --> 15:45.980
I think it was just a cold.

15:46.420 --> 15:49.590
I guess we worried for nothing.

15:49.590 --> 15:50.370
Jeez.

15:50.370 --> 15:52.960
All because Sacchan kept fussing 
that something happened.

15:53.680 --> 15:55.430
Is that what's happening?!

15:55.430 --> 15:57.990
Oh, no, don't worry.

15:57.990 --> 15:59.450
There's nothing to worry about.

16:00.100 --> 16:01.840
Sorry.

16:11.400 --> 16:12.710
Sally-chan...

16:13.710 --> 16:17.450
Could we talk for a bit?

16:17.930 --> 16:20.570
Just the two of us.

16:26.200 --> 16:32.140
Okay, so first, I won't tell 
anyone what we talk about here.

16:26.520 --> 16:28.280
Okay, here we go.

16:32.140 --> 16:33.550
Not even the teachers.

16:34.470 --> 16:40.060
So I want you to be honest about
 what you're feeling right now.

16:40.580 --> 16:42.110
What's weighing you down?

16:44.070 --> 16:46.250
No?

16:54.270 --> 16:55.590
Senpai...

16:56.910 --> 17:01.000
You're close friends with 
Kousaka-senpai, aren't you?

17:01.000 --> 17:02.870
So it is about Reina.

17:06.760 --> 17:15.340
But it's not that I despise her or 
hate her or anything like that.

17:16.810 --> 17:20.240
Actually, Kousaka-senpai is right.

17:20.240 --> 17:25.260
I think this is what it takes if we're 
going to win gold at the Nationals.

17:25.260 --> 17:28.870
We obviously have to work harder.

17:25.720 --> 17:29.270
Your steps are off! 
Keep them together until the end!

17:29.920 --> 17:33.680
But it's the competition members 
that need to, isn't it?

17:33.680 --> 17:37.890
I don't know if the beginners 
need to work so hard.

17:38.350 --> 17:41.910
The beginners look like 
they're having it rough.

17:41.910 --> 17:46.420
I still tried to convince 
them not to quit anyway.

17:47.940 --> 17:51.340
That it'll be fun if we 
work hard and get results.

17:51.650 --> 17:52.820
But...

17:53.770 --> 17:56.330
Practice gets harder and harder.

17:56.330 --> 17:59.540
The beginners are always crying.

17:59.540 --> 18:05.570
I can't help but feel like I did 
something bad when I see that.

18:12.300 --> 18:13.800
Sally-chan...

18:16.220 --> 18:17.660
I'm sorry.

18:22.330 --> 18:23.450
No...

18:26.530 --> 18:27.770
Thanks.

18:30.750 --> 18:34.120
No one's quit yet, thanks to you.

18:34.120 --> 18:35.600
Everyone's still here,

18:35.600 --> 18:37.580
even the first-years.

18:41.330 --> 18:43.620
But that might not be a good thing.

18:44.420 --> 18:48.780
To be honest, I thought the same thing.

18:49.650 --> 18:52.240
That maybe the beginners should be separate.

18:52.610 --> 18:55.730
That we should change the way we practice.

18:56.730 --> 18:58.400
You did?

18:58.400 --> 18:59.240
Yeah.

18:59.980 --> 19:07.540
But I think all of our members want to 
get better to some degree.

19:08.250 --> 19:11.220
Some of them might feel 
like it's just a club.

19:11.020 --> 19:12.750
Straighten your back!

19:11.610 --> 19:13.830
But now that we've committed to it,

19:13.830 --> 19:18.380
we're going to be spending the majority 
of our high school lives on it.

19:18.750 --> 19:23.510
So I don't want to regret it, and 
I don't want others to, either.

19:19.500 --> 19:22.010
I think that was the most 
together we've done it so far.

19:22.010 --> 19:25.230
Everyone's improved on 
the parts I pointed out.

19:23.890 --> 19:26.160
I want people to be glad they did it.

19:27.050 --> 19:29.340
Everyone feels that way.

19:29.780 --> 19:32.720
I don't think it's right 
to burst their bubble.

19:33.020 --> 19:38.510
So I think everyone feels 
encouraged thanks to you.

19:38.510 --> 19:39.490
But then...

19:39.900 --> 19:43.070
You're okay with how things are?

19:43.070 --> 19:44.500
That's the thing...

19:45.200 --> 19:47.420
I don't think so.

19:50.040 --> 19:53.240
Concert band has a lot of people.

19:53.240 --> 19:55.680
There are beginners and advanced players.

19:55.680 --> 19:57.620
People think about things differently.

19:58.140 --> 20:03.310
I think it's hard to find 
one correct answer.

20:03.880 --> 20:05.350
That's the thing.

20:05.960 --> 20:14.530
So I think the president's job is to 
bring everyone's wishes together.

20:16.060 --> 20:17.670
So, yeah...

20:18.550 --> 20:22.840
Bring it all to me.

20:24.090 --> 20:26.250
To you?

20:27.530 --> 20:29.920
Whether it's something 
weighing you down personally,

20:29.920 --> 20:32.150
or some issues the other 
first-years are having...

20:32.580 --> 20:34.050
Tell me everything.

20:34.530 --> 20:38.800
I'm sure everyone has similar problems.

20:40.760 --> 20:44.340
I guess that doesn't solve anything, huh?

20:44.340 --> 20:49.480
But I feel like we can figure 
it out if we talk it through.

21:00.730 --> 21:03.610
National Gold Together!

21:00.730 --> 21:03.610
Hazuki Ririka Suzume Kaho Yayoi

21:00.980 --> 21:02.070
I mean...

21:04.410 --> 21:07.580
We're all aiming for the same goal.

21:17.200 --> 21:19.340
Thanks for having us.

21:20.250 --> 21:21.110
Well?

21:21.840 --> 21:22.920
Yeah.

21:26.480 --> 21:31.430
I'm glad she's the president.

21:33.010 --> 21:34.060
I see.

21:36.300 --> 21:38.620
So, what did you talk about?

21:38.620 --> 21:40.580
Nothing, really.

21:40.580 --> 21:43.760
We need Sally-chan in the club, don't we?

21:44.320 --> 21:45.980
Of course.

21:47.070 --> 21:50.820
Kumiko-senpai likes people who have talent.

21:50.820 --> 21:52.280
I can see that.

21:52.280 --> 21:53.600
Right?

22:05.310 --> 22:09.390
Yoshii-san took the keys earlier.

22:09.390 --> 22:11.010
I see.

22:21.410 --> 22:23.110
Good morning.

22:23.110 --> 22:24.390
Morning.

22:25.960 --> 22:27.270
Senpai...

22:28.110 --> 22:30.300
I look forward to working 
with you again today.

22:36.040 --> 22:38.520
<i>Thank you for yesterday!</i>

22:38.520 --> 22:40.580
<i>For hearing Sally out.</i>

22:41.010 --> 22:42.700
<i>I just listened.</i>

22:43.100 --> 22:47.460
<i>I thought Sally would be 
willing to open up to you.</i>

22:47.750 --> 22:51.230
<i>Was that what you were hoping 
for when you talked to me?</i>

22:51.230 --> 22:52.170
<i>Yes.</i>

22:52.170 --> 22:53.060
<i>Also...</i>

22:53.710 --> 22:57.340
<i>I thought everyone would be worried 
if four of us were absent.</i>

22:57.780 --> 22:58.770
<i>Tee-hee.</i>

23:01.950 --> 23:03.370
Is something wrong?

23:03.370 --> 23:04.190
No.

23:04.190 --> 23:06.420
I was just thinking, you can't 
judge a person by how they look.

23:06.420 --> 23:07.600
Including you.

23:08.870 --> 23:10.110
What does that mean?

23:10.380 --> 23:11.740
Are you insulting me?

23:11.740 --> 23:13.570
It's more of a compliment.

23:13.570 --> 23:14.590
Are you sure?

23:14.590 --> 23:16.580
I'm sure.

23:16.580 --> 23:17.760
I don't trust you.

23:18.680 --> 23:23.090
<i>And the next piece begins.</i>

23:21.960 --> 23:25.960
<b>To be continued</b>
